                                        CREDIT CARD TRANSACTION ANALYTICS
                                PostgreSQL + Power BI | Professional Project Documentation

1. Project Overview
An end-to-end Credit Card Transaction Analytics project using PostgreSQL and Power BI. 
The project transforms credit card transaction data into business insights covering customer behavior, transaction performance, payment modes, card networks, merchants, categories, branches and geographic performance.

2. Business Objectives
•	Measure total transaction amount and transaction volume.
•	Understand customer spending behavior and transaction frequency.
•	Identify repeat, high-spending and high-frequency customers.
•	Analyze approval, decline and reversal patterns.
•	Compare spending across payment modes and card networks.
•	Identify top merchants and high-performing merchant categories.
•	Analyze average transaction value across categories and merchants.
•	Compare branch-level transaction amount, volume and decline performance.
•	Analyze customer distribution by state and transaction spending by city.
•	Build interactive, executive-ready Power BI dashboards.

3. Technology Stack
•	PostgreSQL — data storage, SQL analysis, joins, aggregations and analytical views.
•	DBeaver — database management and SQL development.
•	Power BI — interactive dashboards, KPI cards, visualizations and slicers.
•	CSV — source data and data inspection.
•	GitHub — portfolio presentation and version control.

4. Dataset
Table	           Records	                       Purpose	                                          Key Field
customers        	10,000          	Customer demographic and income information                 	customer_id
cards	            15,000	          Customer card information                                    	card_id / customer_id
merchants	        2,000	            Merchant and category information	                            merchant_id
branches	        250           	  Branch and geographic information	                            branch_id
transactions	    100,000	          Credit card transaction records                              	transaction_id

Data coverage:100,000 transactions across 10,000 customers, 15,000 cards, 2,000 merchants and 250 branches.

5. Data Model & Relationships
The analytical model connects customer, card, transaction, merchant and branch information.
customers.customer_id → cards.customer_id
cards.card_id → transactions.card_id
merchants.merchant_id → transactions.merchant_id
branches.branch_id → transactions.branch_id

customers
    │
    ▼
  cards
    │
    ▼
transactions
   ├──────────────► merchants
   │
   └──────────────► branches


6. Data Preparation & Quality Checks
•	Validated table and column structures using information_schema.
•	Checked transaction, customer, card, merchant and branch record counts.
•	Validated joins between customers, cards and transactions.
•	Checked transaction status values including Approved, Declined and Reversed.
•	Validated transaction dates and monthly date calculations.
•	Checked aggregation logic for transaction amount, transaction count and average transaction value.
•	Validated percentage calculations using decimal division.
•	Verified Top-N ranking logic for customers, merchants and branches.
•	Used SQL views to organize reusable analytical outputs for Power BI.

