9. Power BI Dashboard
The Power BI report contains 5 analytical pages, 18 KPI cards and 25 visualizations.
Page 1 — Executive Overview
•	KPI Cards: Total Transaction Amount, Total Transactions, Average Transaction Value, Approved Transactions, Approval Rate and Decline Rate.
•	Monthly Transaction Amount.
•	Monthly Transaction Volume.
•	Spending by Merchant Category.
•	Spending by Card Type.
•	Top 10 Customers by Spending.
•	Slicers: Year, Card Type and Transaction Status.

Page 2 — Customer Analysis
•	KPI Cards: Total Customers, Repeat Customers and Average Revenue per Customer.
•	Customer Spending by Income.
•	Customer Spending by Gender.
•	Customer Transaction Frequency.
•	Customers by Number of Cards.
•	Top 10 Customers by Transactions.
•	Slicers: Gender, Income Group and State.

Page 3 — Transaction Analysis
•	KPI Cards: Total Transactions, Approved Transactions and Average Transaction Value.
•	Spending by Payment Mode.
•	Transaction Status Distribution.
•	Average Transaction Value by Category.
•	Spending by Card Network.
•	Transactions by State.
•	Slicers: Transaction Status, Payment Mode and Card Network.

Page 4 — Merchant & Category Analysis
•	KPI Cards: Total Merchants, Top Merchant Spending and Average Transaction Value.
•	Top 10 Merchants by Spending.
•	Transaction Volume by Category.
•	Transaction Status by Category.
•	Average Transaction Value by Merchant.
•	Category Spending Contribution.
•	Slicers: Merchant Category, City and Transaction Status.

Page 5 — Geographic & Branch Analysis
•	KPI Cards: Total Branches, Top Branch Spending and Average Branch Transaction Amount.
•	Branch Spending.
•	Branch Transaction Volume.
•	Branch Decline Rate.
•	Customer Distribution by State.
•	Transaction Spending by City.
•	Slicers: State, City and Branch.

10. Key Analytical Insights
•	Transaction value and transaction volume provide complementary views of overall card activity.
•	Approved transactions represent the largest transaction-status group, while declined and reversed transactions provide important operational monitoring signals.
•	Customer spending can be compared across income groups and gender to understand spending concentration.
•	Transaction frequency highlights customers who transact more often and can support customer behavior analysis.
•	Payment mode and card network analysis helps compare transaction value across payment channels.
•	Top merchant analysis identifies merchants that contribute the greatest transaction spending.
•	Category spending contribution shows how individual merchant categories contribute to overall transaction value.
•	Branch and city analysis highlights geographic differences in transaction activity and spending.
•	State-level customer distribution helps identify geographic concentration of the customer base.

11. SQL Techniques Demonstrated
•	SELECT, WHERE and ORDER BY
